  "notes": [
    "Sales tax is charged on the purchase price or the vehicle's current market value, per PennDOT. The calculator uses the price you enter.",
    "A plate transfer costs $11 and a lien costs $36. Not modeled.",
    "Plug-in hybrids pay a road user charge; not modeled.",
    "Private-party sales and gifts follow different rules; not modeled."
  ],
  "content": {
    "intro": "{state} charges {stateRate} sales tax on a vehicle purchase, with an extra local tax in only two places. You also pay a title fee and a registration fee, and electric vehicles pay a separate yearly road user charge.",
    "howItWorks": [
      {
        "text": "The state rate is {stateRate}. Only Allegheny County and the City of Philadelphia add a local sales tax on top, so pick your county and the calculator fills in the extra amount. When a seller takes a vehicle as a trade-in, the tax is charged on the difference between the price and the trade-in value.",
        "sources": [
          "https://www.pa.gov/content/dam/copapwp-pagov/en/penndot/documents/public/dvspubsforms/bmv/bmv-fact-sheets/fs-buysell.pdf",
          "https://www.pa.gov/agencies/revenue/resources/tax-types-and-information/sales-use-and-hotel-occupancy-tax/use-tax/use-tax-for-individuals"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "If you paid tax to another state on the same vehicle, {state} can give credit for it. The credit applies only when the other state gives a similar credit for Pennsylvania tax, and it cannot be more than the Pennsylvania tax due.",
        "sources": [
          "https://www.pa.gov/content/dam/copapwp-pagov/en/revenue/documents/formsandpublications/formsforbusinesses/sut/documents/rev-227.pdf"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Passenger car registration is a flat yearly fee, and the title fee is charged once. Owners of battery electric vehicles also pay a yearly road user charge before they renew. Some counties add a small local fee to registration, which is not in the total because it depends on your county.",
        "sources": [
          "https://www.pa.gov/content/dam/copapwp-pagov/en/penndot/documents/public/dvspubsforms/bmv/bmv-forms/mv-70s.pdf",
          "https://www.pa.gov/agencies/dmv/vehicle-services/road-user-charge",
          "https://www.pa.gov/content/dam/copapwp-pagov/en/penndot/documents/public/dvspubsforms/bmv/bmv-fact-sheets/fs-feelocal.pdf"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "Does a trade-in lower the sales tax in Pennsylvania?",
        "text": "Yes. When a seller takes your vehicle as a trade-in, the tax is charged on the difference between the price of the new vehicle and the trade-in value.",
        "sources": [
          "https://www.pa.gov/content/dam/copapwp-pagov/en/penndot/documents/public/dvspubsforms/bmv/bmv-fact-sheets/fs-buysell.pdf"
        ]
      },
      {
        "q": "Do I pay extra tax in Philadelphia or Allegheny County?",
        "text": "Yes. Both add a local sales and use tax on top of the state rate. Other counties do not.",
        "sources": [
          "https://www.pa.gov/content/dam/copapwp-pagov/en/penndot/documents/public/dvspubsforms/bmv/bmv-fact-sheets/fs-buysell.pdf",
          "https://www.pa.gov/agencies/revenue/resources/tax-types-and-information/sales-use-and-hotel-occupancy-tax/use-tax/use-tax-for-individuals"
        ]
      },
      {
        "q": "What if I bought the vehicle in another state?",
        "text": "Pennsylvania can credit tax you legally paid to another state, but only if that state gives a substantially similar credit. Several states do not, so check the credit chart for the state where you bought.",
        "sources": [
          "https://www.pa.gov/content/dam/copapwp-pagov/en/revenue/documents/formsandpublications/formsforbusinesses/sut/documents/rev-227.pdf"
        ]
      },
      {
        "q": "Do electric vehicles pay an extra fee?",
        "text": "Yes. Battery electric vehicles pay a yearly road user charge, separate from registration. Plug-in hybrids pay a smaller charge, which this calculator does not include.",
        "sources": [
          "https://www.pa.gov/content/dam/copapwp-pagov/en/penndot/documents/public/dvspubsforms/bmv/bmv-forms/mv-70s.pdf",
          "https://www.pa.gov/agencies/dmv/vehicle-services/road-user-charge"
        ]
      },
      {
        "q": "What is the Fee for Local Use?",
        "text": "It is a small yearly fee that participating counties add to vehicle registration. It is left out of the total because it depends on your county.",
        "sources": [
          "https://www.pa.gov/content/dam/copapwp-pagov/en/penndot/documents/public/dvspubsforms/bmv/bmv-fact-sheets/fs-feelocal.pdf"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
